Track 2: Eun-ji at the Annealing Lehr
- Story & Context: Written during a three-week hideout in an abandoned glass factory outside Gimpo, this slow-burn confessional documents bassist Eun-ji Cho’s quiet reckoning with family estrangement and industrial burn-out. The track captures the clinking sound of cooling silicate bottles along the floor, captured by an open condenser mic while Vance plucks a weeping bottleneck riff soaked in tube tremolo. The tension peaked when factory security cornered Cho in the rear furnace room, where she used an insulated screwdriver to tap into the facility's master loudspeaker panel to broadcast her defiant final vocal take: "Cool me slow in the iron box, but you can’t temper what’s already broken."
