Track 3: Did the Blowpipe Crack in the Cold?
- Story & Context: By midwinter, after the state cracked down on highway splices with felony warrants, myth grew around a ghost transmission that allegedly looped across the Namhae Expressway traffic network every midnight without an operator in sight. Truck drivers reported hearing the violent rattle of accordion reeds and distorted Telecaster hum cutting straight through official speed trap advisories, accompanied by the eerie crunch of boots stomping on safety glass. The mythical loop immortalized the final clash between the collective and the riot squads with one last haunting line: "When the frost took our breath, we taught the glass how to scream."
